  "Question": "\\((6 \\ ? \\ 3) + 4 - (2 - 1) = 5.\\) To make this statement true, the question mark between the \\(6\\) and the \\(3\\) should be replaced by",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\div\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\times\\)",
    "C": "\\(+\\)",
    "D": "\\(-\\)",
    "E": "None of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "First evaluate \\(2-1=1\\). The part outside the first parentheses contributes \\(4-1=3\\), so \\(6\\,?\\,3\\) must equal \\(5-3=2\\). Among the listed operations, only division gives \\(6\\div3=2\\). Indeed,\n\\[\n(6\\div3)+4-(2-1)=2+4-1=5.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\div}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
